        "text": "HARBOR ASSET MANAGEMENT\nJanuary 20, 2026\nDear Partners,\nHarbor Credit Opportunities Fund returned 1.70% net in the fourth quarter of\n2025, bringing full-year performance to 7.9% net. Returns were driven by carry\nin our senior secured loan book and by two restructurings that closed ahead of\nschedule.\nPeriod | Net return\nOctober 2025 | 0.58%\nNovember 2025 | 0.62%\nDecember 2025 | 0.49%\nQ4 2025 | 1.70%\nPositioning. Portfolio duration remains short at roughly 1.3 years, as most of the\nbook is floating rate. We see limited exposure to a further move in long-end\nyields, though slower rate cuts would keep coupon income elevated. Default rates\nin our universe ticked up to 3.1%, and we have been avoiding cov-lite deals in\nsoftware and healthcare services.\nOutlook. We expect 2026 to offer better entry points in stressed credit as\nmaturity walls approach. Dry powder stands at 14% of NAV.\nFund AUM at quarter end was $905 million. Liquidity: quarterly redemptions\nwith 90 days' notice.\nSincerely,\nDana Whitlock\nChief Investment Officer\nFictional fund and people for demonstration purposes.\nPage 1"
